\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 # ZA Hackathon Outcome Agent\
\
Canonical date: 29/07/2026  \
Architecture: one product agent, two model roles, one backend entrypoint\
\
## Decision\
\
Replace:\
\
```text\
Backend \'e2\'86\'92 Intake \'e2\'86\'92 Brain \'e2\'86\'92 Finalizer\
```\
\
with:\
\
```text\
Backend \'e2\'86\'92 Outcome Agent (Claude Sonnet)\
             \'e2\'94\'9c\'e2\'94\'80 fast path \'e2\'86\'92 final response\
             \'e2\'94\'94\'e2\'94\'80 conditional reasoning path\
                  \'e2\'86\'92 Research Brain (Claude Opus sub-agent)\
                  \'e2\'86\'92 semantic result\
                  \'e2\'86\'92 Outcome Agent fact-lock + final response\
```\
\
There are two agent definitions:\
\
1. `outcome_agent`: Claude Sonnet 5, low effort, no direct tools.\
2. `research_brain`: Claude Opus 5, medium effort, web and bash tools.\
\
The backend invokes only `outcome_agent`. Research Brain is\
registered in its `multiagent.agents` list and is invoked internally.\
\
## Why this boundary\
\
The Outcome Agent owns repetitive boundary work:\
\
- interpret the latest message against thin state;\
- collect the minimum viable brief;\
- manage group research confirmation;\
- decide whether Brain is necessary;\
- construct the Brain request;\
- validate and render the Brain result;\
- return one final state patch and reply contract.\
\
Research Brain owns judgment:\
\
- design the decision journey;\
- research only the current decision slice;\
- preserve named inventory and evidence;\
- calculate and reconcile money;\
- recommend and return semantic decision data.\
\
This removes duplicated presentation work from Brain and removes semantic\
routing from backend.\
\
## Import order\
\
1. Import `02_planning_brain.json`.\
2. Copy the created Brain agent ID, such as `agent_...`.\
3. Generate the Outcome Agent config:\
\
```bash\
node configure_coordinator.js agent_<PLANNING_BRAIN_ID>\
```\
\
4. Import the generated `01_outcome_agent.json`.\
5. Configure the application to invoke only the Outcome Agent.\
\
The template intentionally contains\
`REPLACE_WITH_PLANNING_BRAIN_AGENT_ID`; do not import it unchanged.\
\
## Minimal backend\
\
```js\
async function onMessage(event) \{\
  const result = JSON.parse(await runManagedAgent(OUTCOME_AGENT_ID, \{\
    user_message: event.text,\
    reference_time: event.timestamp,\
    actor: event.actor,\
    thin_state: await stateStore.get(event.conversationId),\
  \}));\
\
  assertFinalEnvelope(result);\
  await stateStore.patch(event.conversationId, result.state_patch);\
  await stateStore.saveReplyContract(\
    event.conversationId,\
    result.reply_contract,\
  );\
  await sendToZalo(event.conversationId, result.message_to_user);\
\}\
```\
\
`assertFinalEnvelope` only checks:\
\
- valid JSON;\
- `status` is `ready` or `blocked`;\
- non-empty `message_to_user`;\
- `state_patch`, `reply_contract` and `execution` exist.\
\
Backend must not:\
\
- classify intent;\
- inspect brief completeness;\
- validate group research confirmation;\
- call Brain or a Finalizer;\
- merge state from several agent outputs;\
- run a custom tool loop;\
- reformat the message.\
\
## Technical responsibilities that remain in backend\
\
These cannot safely be delegated to a model:\
\
- authentication and authorization;\
- one active managed run per conversation;\
- idempotency/deduplication by message ID;\
- timeout and retry policy;\
- JSON parsing and schema validation;\
- atomic state persistence;\
- sending the final Zalo message;\
- logs, metrics and redaction.\
\
Recommended runtime limits:\
\
- Outcome Agent fast path: 10\'e2\'80\'9320 seconds.\
- Outcome Agent with Brain: target 30\'e2\'80\'9360 seconds.\
- Hard timeout: 90 seconds.\
- One retry only for transport/runtime failure, never semantic disagreement.\
\
## Unified final envelope\
\
Every Outcome Agent run returns:\
\
```json\
\{\
  "status": "ready",\
  "message_to_user": "One Zalo plain-text message",\
  "reply_contract": \{\
    "expected_type": "option_selection",\
    "valid_values": ["transport_01", "transport_02"],\
    "examples": ["Ch\'e1\'bb\uc0\u141 n 1", "Ch\'e1\'bb\u141 n 2"],\
    "expires_with_flow_stage": "choosing_transport"\
  \},\
  "state_patch": \{\},\
  "execution": \{\
    "brain_used": true,\
    "brain_task": "initial_research",\
    "reason_code": "confirmed_scope_requires_research",\
    "scope_version": 1\
  \}\
\}\
```\
\
The backend always handles the same shape, whether Brain was used or not.\
\
## Brain internal contract\
\
Brain receives a normalized `brain_request` from Outcome Agent and returns:\
\
- `answer_payload`: semantic result;\
- `decision_summary`: recommendation and caveats;\
- `state_delta`: stable mappings and next decision;\
- `evidence` and `calculations`;\
- `quality`.\
\
Brain never returns user-facing prose. Outcome Agent fact-locks the result and\
merges `state_delta` into its one final `state_patch`.\
\
## Conditional delegation\
\
Sonnet does not call Opus merely because the message is a selection or\
follow-up. It first checks whether the turn can be handled from the verified\
thin state.\
\
Call Opus only when the turn needs at least one of:\
\
- multi-source live research;\
- recommendation under several binding constraints;\
- reconciliation of conflicting candidates or evidence;\
- multi-step planning/replanning with dependencies;\
- deterministic non-trivial cost/split calculation;\
- explicit deep research;\
- judgment that Sonnet cannot provide confidently without guessing.\
\
Do not call Opus for:\
\
- greeting, clarification, scope confirmation or cancellation;\
- stable quick QA;\
- resolving a visible label to a stored stable ID;\
- repeating or formatting a verified plan;\
- a follow-up already answered by verified state;\
- a selection that does not require research for the next decision.\
\
## Thin state\
\
Persist only:\
\
```json\
\{\
  "active_flow": \{\
    "type": "trip",\
    "stage": "gathering|awaiting_research_confirmation|researching|choosing_transport|choosing_stay|choosing_activity|completed|cancelled",\
    "scope_version": 1,\
    "confirmed_scope_version": 1,\
    "research_status": "idle|running|completed|failed"\
  \},\
  "current_brief": \{\},\
  "unresolved_blockers": [],\
  "candidate_mappings": [\
    \{\
      "decision_id": "transport",\
      "candidate_id": "transport_01",\
      "visible_label": "1",\
      "summary": "short"\
    \}\
  ],\
  "current_decision": \{\},\
  "selected_id": null,\
  "last_decision_summary": \{\},\
  "reply_contract": \{\}\
\}\
```\
\
Do not persist full evidence pages, web content, transcript or reasoning.\
\
## Group research confirmation\
\
The exact phrase `B\'e1\'ba\'aeT \'c4\uc0\u144 \'e1\'ba\'a6U RESEARCH` confirms research for the current scope.\
Any group member may send it. It is not authorization to book, pay, cancel,\
send a provider message or modify a calendar.\
\
Material changes to destination, dates, budget, participants, outcome or hard\
constraints increment `scope_version` and require confirmation again.\
\
## Brain performance\
\
Research Brain preserves the v8.1 latency contract:\
\
- one turn, one decision slice;\
- two candidates by default;\
- initial/replan cap: 2 search, 3 fetch, 1 bash;\
- follow-up/selection cap: 1 search, 2 fetch, 1 bash;\
- output target 3.5\'e2\'80\'936K tokens, hard cap 8K;\
- no pre-research of future shopping slots;\
- reuse valid state and research only delta.\
\
## Nested specialists\
\
Do not add specialist agents for the hackathon default. They increase import\
dependencies and latency.\
\
If later needed, specialists must be registered inside Research Brain's managed\
run. The backend contract stays unchanged. Brain remains accountable for one\
semantic result and must keep the same tool/output budget.\
\
## Failure behavior\
\
- Invalid handoff: Brain makes no tool call and returns to Outcome Agent.\
- Tool unavailable or insufficient evidence: Outcome Agent sends a short,\
  honest blocked/partial message.\
- Timeout: backend sends one generic technical fallback and marks\
  `research_status=failed`; it does not invent a plan.\
- Malformed JSON: one technical retry, then fail closed.\
\
## Migration from v8\
\
Delete from runtime:\
\
- the separate Finalizer agent;\
- backend `target=deliver|brain` branching;\
- backend Brain gate;\
- backend state merge across Intake, Brain and Finalizer;\
- `ready_for_finalizer`;\
- `message_to_user` or `draft_message_to_user` in Brain;\
- owner identification;\
- custom-tool adapters.\
\
Keep:\
\
- minimum viable brief;\
- group research confirmation;\
- named inventory;\
- slot-by-slot decision journey;\
- deterministic money calculation;\
- one-decision-slice latency contract;\
- stable reply mappings.\
}